        "Whatever the explanation, the placebo effect offers an important lesson for medicine. Treating illness is not only a matter of chemistry. {u:⑶:How patients understand their condition, and how they are treated as people, can make a measurable difference to how they feel.} This does not mean that real drugs are unnecessary, or that serious diseases can be cured by belief alone. It means that good communication should be ({b:43}) as part of good care, not as something extra. Doctors who take time to explain, to listen, and to {u:⑷:set realistic expectations} may be ({b:44}) the power of the placebo effect without any deception at all — and ({b:45}) the risks of the nocebo effect at the same time.",
